{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0440-leap-likelihood-elicitation-and-aggregation-for.md", "equation": "Two-stage decomposition: collection stage yields evidence set E={e1…en}; prediction stage maps (T,E)→forecast. LEAP's prediction stage: (1) Prior elicitation — parameters of P0 from historical data when available (e.g., recent market prices), otherwise one blind LLM call with no evidence (prompt forbids conditioning on evidence to avoid double-counting). For discrete tasks without a base rate, a uniform conservative prior. (2) Per-evidence likelihood elicitation — one isolated LLM call per evidence item (the call sees T and only ei; never other items or partial posteriors) returning a structured schema: for continuous targets a target-scale observation µi with σi from a fixed metadata map; for single-choice, qualitative support labels per option mapped to non-normalized likelihoods Li(k)=P(ei|θ=k); for multi-choice, support/opposition labels mapped to log-likelihood ratios. Reliability s ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9126}
