{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0446-minimaxity-and-admissibility-of-bayesian-neural.md", "equation": "Verdict:** ADAPT — the fixed-scale BNN non-minimaxity mechanism (heavy over-shrinkage of large signals from too-thin prior tails, with depth delaying but not removing the failure) and the BetaPrime hyperprior repair are directly portable to GSE's high-dimensional shrinkage problems: team/player effect estimates and multi-market probability blending where a thin-tailed global prior would over-shrink the biggest true signals; the radial shrinkage rule δ(Y)=(1−E[(1+W)^{−1}|Y])Y is a reimplementable calibrator, not abstract theory.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9126}
